  "description_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"courseDescription\">\n    Prerequisites: JOUR 3173 and JOUR 3273. \n\nPresents the elements of effective print design as well as the other decision making processes involved with creating an effective visual communication (type, art and illustration, basic design principles, paper and ink, printing processes, etc.). Students will create visually appealing projects using the industry standard design and photo manipulation software programs.\n    \n</section>",
